{"narrative": "As you keep your rifle ready and move aft, your boots thump softly against the frost-covered deck. The corridor stretches long, it's concave sides loom into darkness. The tapping grows louder with each step you take. Sharp, metallic, rhythm-less; it’s a quiet symphony of neglect.

Ahead, in the dimness, a soft, spectral glow of a malfunctioning console light casts an eerie pallor. The source of the tapping is just around the corner. You pause, listening, and the only sound that fills the silence is the stuttering tick of cooling metal; Nothing that breathes.

 A greasy smell hangs in the air, faint but unmistakable - an odor of machine oil and old dust. At the edge of your senses, you notice another smell. Something cold, biological. Reminiscent of a butcher's shop left unattended for too long.", "choices": ["Turn the corner quickly, rifle at the ready", "Use your olef A13 laser pistol to check the corner from a distance", "Call out to anyone or anything that might be there", "Retreat and go check the bridge instead"], "dice_rolls": [], "state_updates": {}}

{"narrative":"You step carefully over debris, the muzzle of your imaginary rifle sweeping ahead out of instinct. The frozen air prickles your skin, and the floor vibrates subtly beneath your boots. Each footstep crunches on frost, echoing in the stillness as you make your way aft toward the rhythmic metallic tapping.

The corridor narrows around you, darkness pressing on the edges of the emergency lighting. The tapping sound grows louder and more erratic—a loose panel barely hanging onto its hinges. Underneath it, you hear a faint, irregular wheezing, almost drowned out by the shifting hull. Is it a survivor—or something else forced in by the breach?

You notice a broken maintenance hatch nearby and scattered power cells glinting by your feet. If you improvise, you might fashion something to defend yourself or signal others, since your actual rifle was lost in the chaos. Nearby, a battered comm-unit blinks feebly, caught between static and a garbled transmission.","dice_rolls":[],"state_updates":{"stamina_delta":0,"seu_delta":0,"seu_source":null,"ammo_updates":{},"status_add":[],"status_remove":[],"inventory_add":[],"inventory_remove":[],"xp_delta":0,"credits_delta":0,"npc_updates":[],"faction_updates":[],"journal_entry":null,"scene_id":null},"choices":[{"id":"investigate_panel","text":"Quietly investigate the panel, ready to improvise if needed.","action_type":"investigate"},{"id":"jury_rig_defense","text":"Quickly use your knack for improvisation to jury-rig a defensive device from the hatch and spare power cells (Signature Trait).","action_type":"use_signature_trait"},{"id":"comm_unit","text":"Examine and try to repair the malfunctioning comm-unit to contact survivors or call for help.","action_type":"tech"},{"id":"withdraw","text":"Withdraw and rejoin the others, reporting what you've found.","action_type":"move"}],"scene_change":false,"scene_header":null,"scene_summary":"Kael advances aft toward the sound, encountering evidence of possible survivors, makeshift tools, and a failing comm-unit.","combat_state_update":null,"ooc_note":null,"tooltip_terms":[]}

{"narrative":"You keep your pistol up and push aft along the tilted aisle, boots skidding on scorched plating. Red strobes smear across smoke, the heat tastes like copper, and the tapping sharpens into a steady tick from the starboard wall, now your floor. Beneath a buckled row of crash seats, you catch a thin, wet wheeze and see fingers twitching through torn fabric beside a jagged slit of purple daylight.

Dr. Orvaine staggers in your wake, sleeve over her mouth. Vriktik points a chitinous limb at a humming conduit overhead, cool mist beading along it. “Coolant spine. Crack it right, we drown the fire,” he rasps. Squelb hugs a glossy cargo blanket like a contract, eyes wide. “I can pay you to prioritize me,” he squeaks, as the engine bay coughs a warning boom.

Heat surges, the hull groans, and the ticking turns frantic. The trapped survivor’s breath falters, flames lick higher, and every second feels expensive. Your edge here is not protocol, it is whatever works with what you have, fast.","dice_rolls":[{"description":"Listen for breathing in the smoke","target":40,"roll":27,"success":true,"rule_source":null},{"description":"Navigate the tilted, burning aisle without mishap","target":55,"roll":33,"success":true,"rule_source":null}],"state_updates":{"stamina_delta":0,"seu_delta":0,"seu_source":null,"ammo_updates":{},"status_add":[],"status_remove":[],"inventory_add":[],"inventory_remove":[],"xp_delta":0,"credits_delta":0,"npc_updates":[],"faction_updates":[],"journal_entry":null,"scene_id":null},"choices":[{"id":"improv_coolant_flood","text":"Jam the vibe knife into the coolant spine and lash it with seat webbing to fog the aisle, starving the flames and clearing a path.","action_type":"skill:improvisation"},{"id":"free_trapped","text":"Wedge the knife as a pry bar and rip the buckled seat free to pull the breathing survivor out now.","action_type":"strength"},{"id":"blanket_push","text":"Grab Squelb’s cargo blanket as a heat shield and bull through the smoke to reach the survivor, ordering the others to follow.","action_type":"leadership"},{"id":"bail_outside","text":"Abort the aft, herd everyone through the hull breach into the purple daylight before the engine bay goes up.","action_type":"move"}],"scene_change":false,"scene_header":null,"scene_summary":"Inside the burning, tilted shuttle, Kael pinpoints a trapped survivor by a buckled seat while fire spreads. A nearby coolant conduit could smother the flames; escape through a hull breach is possible but risky with someone still trapped.","combat_state_update":null,"ooc_note":null,"tooltip_terms":[]}

